module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.cross_type_comparison_answers_instead_of_refusing

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data cross_type_comparison_answers_instead_of_refusing: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "cross_type_comparison_answers_instead_of_refusing" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an equality or ordering whose two operands have DIFFERENT types is accepted and ANSWERS, rather than being refused. The observed instance compares a Measure record against a bare integer literal -- `o == 4104` where o is a ByteSize -- and evaluates FALSE. std.measure declares ByteSize = Measure<Memory, One, Nat> and Measure is a RECORD with a count field, so this is not two numeric types that might plausibly unify: it is a record against a scalar, maximally distinguishable, with both operand types present at the site.",
    "HARM, AND IT INVERTS WITH CONTEXT, which is why the two receipts below look like different bugs. In an ASSERTION an always-false comparison is LOUD: the witness goes red and the author finds it. In a GUARD -- `if x == y { refuse } else { proceed }` -- the refusal NEVER FIRES and the program proceeds silently forever. Same defect, opposite visibility: in a test it is a red, in a wall it is a wall that does not exist. That is the fail-open outcome DESIGN section 5 names as the worst one, reached through the type system rather than through a degraded failure arm.",
    "RECEIPT ONE, gunbc#11193: converting safetensors_shard_declared_overhead from Nat to ByteSize (a review finding -- derived byte quantities belong in the unit carrier) left a witness comparing the now-ByteSize binding against the literal 4104. The compile-clean gate returned ZERO BLOCKING ERRORS ON EVERY ENTRY. The suite then returned 53/1. Nothing located the site; it was found by the assertion being false.",
    "RECEIPT TWO, same PR, opposite direction and this is the one that makes it a class rather than an incident. A ModelArtifact record literal was written with five of the type's six fields; the compile gate accepted it, and it failed only at RUNTIME on first READ, as `no field 'upstream_total' on type 'ModelArtifact'`. Both are type-correct at the DEFINITION and silently wrong at a DISTANT USE, and both are invisible to the gate.",
    "THE TWO DISTINGUISHING FACTS ARE DIFFERENT AND A READER MATCHING ON ONE WILL MISS THE OTHER. The missing field fails at runtime on first read WITH A LOCATED DIAGNOSTIC, so any execution reaching the read discovers it. The cross-type comparison NEVER FAILS and merely returns FALSE, so it is discoverable only by an execution whose EXPECTED value differs from false -- which is why the guard form is undetectable by running the program at all.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The only thing that caught either instance was a suite that happened to exercise the affected fold. A migration touching folds with no exercising control ships silently, and the guard form has no exercising control by construction.",
    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE, and the reason it is not merely a ratchet is that the property is DECIDABLE -- both operand types are present in the Node tree at the comparison site, with no inference problem and no undecidable predicate. DESIGN section 4 derives operations from INHABITANCE rather than per-type definitions, so equality between two types that do not jointly inhabit it has NO INSTANCE: the expression is not a check that fails but a thing with no meaning to construct. A census lens over comparison sites would be rung 2 and is explicitly NOT the target, because section 5 forbids a check that restates a constraint the model already carries.",
    "NEXT TRIGGER, stated as the CAPABILITY rather than as an artifact: `==` and the ordering operators requiring their operands to JOINTLY INHABIT the relation, so a mismatched pair is refused at acceptance rather than answered at runtime. A lens that reports mismatched comparison sites does not retire this row; it would leave the invalid state writable and depend on the lens executing and staying enrolled.",
    "THE FAIL-OPEN FORM IS ADMITTED BUT NOT REALISED AT gunbc#11193's head, and that is a SURVEY RESULT rather than an assumption. Two mechanical passes over dag/ and src/v2: (1) every call to a function whose declared return is one of the 61 Measure carriers, compared against a bare literal -- ZERO sites; (2) every pattern binding of a unit-typed field, resolved through its constructor's own declaration, compared against a bare literal within the arm -- ONE candidate, at test.claim.node_power_envelope_witness_test, inspected by hand and FALSE: the binding is from rank_count, a plain Nat, and the genuinely unit-typed sibling in that same arm is compared correctly through its accessor, megatransfers_per_second_count. So no inert guard was found. This establishes that the class ADMITS the fail-open form, not that the corpus contains one.",
    "AND THE SURVEY'S OWN LIMIT IS PART OF THE FINDING. A first pass keying on NAMES returned 2561 suspect sites and was almost entirely generic-name conflation -- a `k`, `count` or `value` that is unit-typed in one scope and a plain Nat in another. Names in this substrate are scoped and a global name census cannot resolve them, so a grep-shaped audit cannot answer the guard question in general; it can only clear the two shapes above. That is precisely why the class sits at mitigatable: the audit that would make it mechanically preventable needs the compiler's own type resolution, which is the same capability the next trigger names.",
    "REVIEW TELL, for the form a reader can catch without the wall: a comparison where exactly ONE side is unwrapped -- `x == 42` or `x == y` where only y passes through an accessor like byte_size_count or measure_count. One-sided unwrapping is where a derived quantity escaped its type. The adjacent authoring rule that produces this class: a TRANSCRIBED upstream value keeps the source's type, while a quantity DERIVED from it -- a difference of two offsets, a product of elements and width -- is this repository's to type, and leaving it bare is what forces the unwrapping in the first place.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
